cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Galaxy-Based MAG Reconstruction Workflow from Raw Metagenomic Reads: Version 1.0 — Assembly, Coverage Estimation and Genome-Binning Demonstration"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shokunbi
    given-names: Aminat Olamide
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
repository-code: "https://github.com/AminatShokunbi/Metagenomic-MAG-Reconstruction-Galaxy"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - metagenomics
  - MAG reconstruction
  - Galaxy
  - MEGAHIT
  - MetaBAT2
  - genome binning
  - bioinformatics
abstract: >-
  A reproducible Galaxy-based training workflow documenting public metagenomic
  read retrieval, quality control, preprocessing, metagenomic assembly,
  assembly assessment, read recruitment, contig-depth estimation, and an
  initial coverage-informed MetaBAT2 genome-binning attempt. Version 1.0
  transparently records that no genome bins were recovered from the six
  demonstration assemblies and does not claim successful MAG recovery.
